                </table>
            </div>

            <h2>Multi-Node Scaling</h2>
            <div class="table-scroll">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">1 Node</th><th scope="col">2 Nodes</th><th scope="col">4 Nodes</th><th scope="col">Scaling Efficiency</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><th scope="row">Llama 3.1 70B (tok/s)</th><td class="num">—</td><td class="num">34</td><td class="num">28</td><td class="num">82%</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">Qwen 2.5 72B (tok/s)</th><td class="num">—</td><td class="num">31</td><td class="num">26</td><td class="num">84%</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">DeepSeek V2 236B (tok/s)</th><td class="num">—</td><td class="num">—</td><td class="num">19</td><td class="num">—</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h2>Methodology</h2>
            <div class="method-grid">
                <div class="method-card">
                    <h3>Hardware</h3>
                    <p>All benchmarks run on Ubuntu 22.04, CUDA 12.4, NVIDIA driver 550+. GPUs at stock clocks. 10GbE LAN for multi-node tests.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="method-card">
                    <h3>Workload</h3>
                    <p>Input: 512 tokens, output: 128 tokens. 100 requests with 10 concurrent. Warm-up of 10 requests discarded.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="method-card">
                    <h3>Measurement</h3>
                    <p>tok/s = output tokens / generation time (excludes prefill). Latency = time-to-first-token for streaming. Cost uses electricity at $0.30/kWh.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="method-card">
                    <h3>Reproducibility</h3>
                    <p>Run <code style="background:var(--surface);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-family:var(--font-mono)">distllm benchmark run</code> to reproduce. Results in <code style="background:var(--surface);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-family:var(--font-mono)">benchmarks/</code> directory.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="note">
                <strong>Note:</strong> Performance varies by driver version, CUDA version, system load, and network conditions. These numbers represent best-case scenarios with optimal configuration. See the <a href="https://github.com/distributed-llm/distributed-llm/tree/main/benchmarks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--green)">benchmark repository</a> for raw data and scripts.
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

