            <main id="main" class="docs-content">
                <h1>Documentation</h1>
                <p>Everything you need to run distributed LLM inference with DistLLM.</p>

                <h2 id="installation">Installation</h2>
                <pre><code># Core package
pip install distributed-llm

# Self-hosted model loading
pip install "distributed-llm[self-hosted]"

# vLLM, SGLang, and llama.cpp backends
pip install "distributed-llm[backends]"

# All extras
pip install "distributed-llm[all]"</code></pre>

                <h2 id="quick-start">Quick Start</h2>
                <pre><code># 1. Start coordinator and API
distllm cluster start --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-7B --qr

# 2. Join workers on the same LAN
distllm cluster join --discover

# 3. Or run a single-node API for development
distllm system api --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B --local --no-auth

# 4. Query the OpenAI-compatible API
curl http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"meta-llama/Llama-3.2-7B","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Hello!"}]}'</code></pre>

                <h2 id="configuration">Configuration</h2>
                <p>DistLLM uses YAML configuration with environment variable overrides:</p>
                <pre><code># config.yaml
model:
  name: "meta-llama/Llama-3.2-7B"
  dtype: "float16"

coordinator:
  host: "0.0.0.0"
  port: 50050
  api_port: 8000

tls:
  enabled: true
  cert_dir: "certs"</code></pre>
                <p>Environment variables override YAML: <code>DISTLLM_MODEL_NAME</code>, <code>DISTLLM_COORDINATOR_HOST</code>, etc.</p>

                <h2 id="architecture">Architecture</h2>
                <p>DistLLM uses a coordinator-worker architecture with pipeline parallelism:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Coordinator</strong> — API server, request scheduling, node management, health monitoring</li>
                    <li><strong>Workers</strong> — Execute model layers on local GPUs, report health to coordinator</li>
                    <li><strong>Pipeline</strong> — Hidden states flow from worker to worker through the model layers</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 id="pipeline-parallelism">Pipeline Parallelism</h2>
                <p>The model is split across devices by layers. Start the coordinator, then let workers join with automatically assigned or manually provided layer ranges.</p>
                <pre><code># Start coordinator
distllm cluster start --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-7B --port 50050 --api-port 8000

# Worker with explicit layer assignment
distllm cluster join --coordinator 192.168.1.100 --port 50050 \
  --start-layer 0 --end-layer 15 --total-layers 80</code></pre>

                <h2 id="auto-discovery">Auto-Discovery</h2>
                <p>On trusted LANs, DistLLM can discover worker nodes with mDNS so operators do not have to hand-edit coordinator IPs for every machine.</p>
                <pre><code># Coordinator
distllm cluster start --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-7B --qr

# Workers
distllm cluster join --discover</code></pre>

                <h2 id="chat-completions">Chat Completions API</h2>
                <p>OpenAI-compatible endpoint at <code>/v1/chat/completions</code>:</p>
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><th scope="row"><code>model</code></th><td>string</td><td>Model name (HuggingFace ID)</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row"><code>messages</code></th><td>array</td><td>Chat messages</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row"><code>stream</code></th><td>boolean</td><td>Enable streaming</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row"><code>temperature</code></th><td>float</td><td>Sampling temperature (0-2)</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row"><code>max_tokens</code></th><td>integer</td><td>Max tokens to generate</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <h2 id="embeddings">Embeddings API</h2>
                <p>Embedding requests use the OpenAI-compatible <code>/v1/embeddings</code> endpoint when an embedding-capable model is loaded.</p>
                <pre><code>curl http://localhost:8000/v1/embeddings \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5","input":"distributed inference"}'</code></pre>

                <h2 id="health">Health Checks</h2>
                <p>Use health endpoints for load balancers, Kubernetes probes, and operational dashboards.</p>
                <pre><code>curl http://localhost:8000/health
curl http://localhost:8000/v1/health/readiness
curl http://localhost:8000/v1/health/liveness
curl http://localhost:8000/metrics</code></pre>

                <h2 id="docker">Docker Deployment</h2>
                <pre><code># docker-compose.yml
services:
  coordinator:
    image: ghcr.io/distributed-llm/coordinator:latest
    ports: ["8000:8000", "50050:50050"]
  worker:
    image: ghcr.io/distributed-llm/worker:latest
    deploy:
      resources:
        reservations:
          devices: [{capabilities: [gpu]}]</code></pre>

                <h2 id="kubernetes">Kubernetes Deployment</h2>
                <p>Run the coordinator behind a service and workers as GPU-scheduled deployments or daemonsets. Use readiness probes before routing production traffic.</p>
                <pre><code>helm install distllm ./integrations/kubernetes/helm/distllm \
  --set model.name=meta-llama/Llama-3.2-7B \
  --set workers.replicas=3</code></pre>

                <h2 id="multi-node">Multi-Node Deployment</h2>
                <p>For multiple physical machines, keep coordinator and workers on a low-latency network, enable TLS, and size layer partitions by each node's available VRAM.</p>
                <pre><code># Coordinator
distllm cluster start --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-70B --port 50050 --api-port 8000 --qr

# Workers
distllm cluster join --coordinator 192.168.1.100 --port 50050

# API-only local development
distllm system api --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B --local --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --no-auth</code></pre>

                <h2 id="models">Model Compatibility</h2>
                <p>The repository includes a compatibility matrix for Llama, Mistral, Mixtral, Qwen, DeepSeek, Falcon, Phi, Gemma, and CodeLlama, plus backend and quantization guidance.</p>
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model Size</th><th scope="col">Recommended Minimum</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><th scope="row">7-8B</th><td>8GB VRAM</td><td>Runs on common consumer GPUs.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">34B</th><td>24GB VRAM</td><td>RTX 4090/A5000 class, or split across nodes.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">70B</th><td>48GB+ pooled VRAM</td><td>Typically 2-4 GPUs with quantization options.</td></tr>
                        <tr><th scope="row">405B</th><td>160GB+ pooled VRAM</td><td>Large multi-node setups.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <h2 id="performance">Performance Tuning</h2>
                <p>DistLLM exposes tuning flags for pipeline overlap, PagedAttention, chunked prefill, KV cache quantization, activation compression, and WAN transport.</p>
                <pre><code>export DISTLLM_ENABLE_PIPELINE_OVERLAP=true
export DISTLLM_PAGED_ATTENTION=true
export DISTLLM_CHUNKED_PREFILL=true
export DISTLLM_KV_CACHE_QUANT_BITS=8

distllm benchmark run --model llama-3-8b
distllm benchmark compare --baseline results/baseline.json</code></pre>

                <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
                <p>For production, enable TLS, API keys, cluster keys, rate limiting, audit logging, restricted CORS, and firewall rules.</p>
                <pre><code>export API_KEY="$(python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))')"
export DISTLLM_CLUSTER_KEY="shared-cluster-secret"

distllm security cert create --hostname my-cluster.example.com
distllm system api --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B --local</code></pre>

                <h2 id="observability">Observability</h2>
                <p>The repo includes Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry, SLO reporting, and scheduler visualization assets.</p>
                <pre><code>distllm system observe
distllm system slo-report
distllm system schedule-viz --output schedule.html</code></pre>

                <h2 id="integrations">Integrations</h2>
                <p>DistLLM includes integration packages and examples for LangChain, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, Haystack, LiteLLM, AutoGen, Semantic Kernel, OpenWebUI, Dify, Ollama compatibility, FastAPI middleware, Kubernetes, Terraform, Ansible, and Grafana.</p>

                <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/distributed-llm/distributed-llm/tree/main/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">full documentation on GitHub</a> for more details.</p>
            </main>
        </div>
    </div>
