        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section class="section section-alt" id="faq">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="sec-h fade-up"><div class="tag">FAQ</div><h2>Common questions</h2></div>
                <div class="faq-list fade-up">
                    <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" id="faq-q-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-1"><span>What GPUs are supported?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a" id="faq-a-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-1"><div class="faq-a-inner">Any NVIDIA GPU with CUDA 12+ (RTX 30xx, 40xx, A100, H100), AMD via ROCm, Apple Silicon via Metal, CPU-only via llama.cpp.</div></div></div>
                    <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" id="faq-q-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-2"><span>How does it compare to vLLM?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a" id="faq-a-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-2"><div class="faq-a-inner">vLLM is excellent for single-node inference. DistLLM differentiator is <strong>multi-node pipeline parallelism</strong>. If your model fits on one GPU, vLLM may be faster. If it doesn't, use DistLLM. DistLLM also supports vLLM as a backend.</div></div></div>
                    <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" id="faq-q-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-3"><span>Is my data safe?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a" id="faq-a-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-3"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes. All data stays on your devices. DistLLM supports mTLS, E2E encryption, and standard authentication. No data sent to any cloud service unless explicitly configured.</div></div></div>
                    <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" id="faq-q-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-4"><span>Can I run it over the internet?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a" id="faq-a-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-4"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes. WAN support with QUIC transport, NAT traversal (STUN/TURN), and token accumulation. LAN is always faster though.</div></div></div>
                    <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" id="faq-q-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-5"><span>What models are supported?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a" id="faq-a-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-5"><div class="faq-a-inner">Any HuggingFace model: Llama 2/3, Mistral, Mixtral, Qwen, Phi, DeepSeek, StableLM, GPT-2, and more. Loaded via <code>AutoModel</code> and auto-partitioned by VRAM.</div></div></div>
                    <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" id="faq-q-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-6"><span>How do I get started?</span><span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a" id="faq-a-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-6"><div class="faq-a-inner"><code>pip install distributed-llm</code>, then <code>distllm cluster start --model meta-llama/Llama-3.2-7B</code>, then <code>distllm cluster join</code> on other machines. See the <a href="https://github.com/distributed-llm/distributed-llm#getting-started" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quick Start guide</a>.</div></div></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Roadmap -->
        <section class="section section-alt" id="roadmap">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="sec-h fade-up"><div class="tag">Roadmap</div><h2>What's coming next</h2></div>
                <div class="roadmap-grid fade-up">
                    <div class="roadmap-item roadmap-done"><div class="roadmap-status">&#10004;</div><div><h3>Pipeline Parallelism</h3><p>Split models across devices by layers. Shipped in v0.4.0.</p></div></div>
                    <div class="roadmap-item roadmap-done"><div class="roadmap-status">&#10004;</div><div><h3>OpenAI-Compatible API</h3><p>Drop-in replacement for OpenAI. Shipped in v0.3.0.</p></div></div>
                    <div class="roadmap-item roadmap-done"><div class="roadmap-status">&#10004;</div><div><h3>Auto-Discovery (mDNS)</h3><p>Devices find each other on LAN automatically. Shipped in v0.4.0.</p></div></div>
                    <div class="roadmap-item roadmap-progress"><div class="roadmap-status">&#9201;</div><div><h3>Speculative Decoding</h3><p>EAGLE-2, n-gram, multi-draft. In progress.</p></div></div>
